Day 56 /100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge
Today, I solved LeetCode 124 -(Binary Tree Maximum Path Sum)
-Approach
The key idea is to use Postorder DFS first process the left and right subtrees, then calculate the result for the current node.

For every node:
 Find the maximum contribution from the left subtree.
 Find the maximum contribution from the right subtree.
 Ignore negative contributions using Math.max(childSum, 0).
 Calculate the maximum path passing through the current node:
node.val + left + right
 Update the global maximum answer.

-Time Complexity: O(n)
Each node is visited exactly once.
-Space Complexity: O(h)
Due to the recursion stack, where h is the height of the tree. In the worst case, this becomes O(n).

- Key Takeaway
Today's problem helped me understand an important Binary Tree pattern:
Postorder Traversal + Recursion + Global Maximum
Instead of trying to calculate every possible path separately, we use information from the subtrees to build the optimal solution at each node.
